{"type":"message","id":"72e733b1","parentId":"1a070dcd","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:09:44.305Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Blueprint, a construction document intelligence engine. Your job is to do a FULL DETAILED QUANTITY TAKEOFF for the HHC Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition project.\n\n## Context\n- Project: HHC Bellevue Hospital, Project #11202402, ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- All drawings have been extracted to PNG images at: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_001.png through page_134.png\n- Drawing text extracted to: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/text/\n- Sheet classification: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/classification.json\n- Sheet index (sheet number → page): /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/sheet_index.json\n- Key sheets: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/key_sheets.json\n- Specs summary: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/specs/specs_summary.json\n- Full spec text: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/specs/spec_full_text.txt\n- Project synthesis: /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/synthesis/\n- Bid sheet reference (132 line items): /tmp/bellevue_refresh/Bellevue - Ambulance Drop Off/Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay - Bid Sheet.xlsx\n- BluePrint skill reference: /home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/SKILL.md\n\n## Your Task\n1. Read the SKILL.md for full pipeline instructions\n2. Read the sheet_index.json and classification.json to know which sheets to examine\n3. For EACH line item that needs quantities (non-LS items: Concrete SF, Masonry LF, Steel LF, Sheathing SF, Waterproofing/Insulation/Roofing SF, Doors EA, Storefronts EA, Glazing SF, GWB SF, Tiling SF, Painting SF, Wall Protection SF, Countertops SF, Bicycle Racks EA, Roof Drains EA, Flood Barriers EA, Access Doors EA):\n   - Examine the relevant drawing pages (use the image tool to look at PNGs)\n   - Cross-reference with spec text for that CSI section\n   - Extract quantities with clear documentation of WHERE each number came from\n4. For LS items: provide scope notes describing what's included\n5. Create a comprehensive takeoff report at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/TAKEOFF_REPORT.md\n6. Create a JSON file at /home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/quantities.json mapping each item number to {qty, unit, source_sheets, notes, confidence}\n7. Flag anything you can't determine with HIGH confidence — note what's missing\n\nFocus on the architectural sheets (A-series), structural (S, FO series), and finish schedules. Key sheets: A-101 (floor plan), A-501 (RCP), A-701 (door schedule), A-801 (finish schedule), AD-101 (demo).\n\nBe thorough. This is for a real bid."},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1770062984303}}
{"type":"message","id":"9a25b245","parentId":"72e733b1","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:09:49.643Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me start by reading the key reference files to understand the project structure and bid sheet.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Let me begin by reading the key reference files to understand the project scope and structure."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01YJcApHPzjiE6fsVgXufQSP","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/skills/blueprint/SKILL.md","limit":100}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01MA8vFKnA5c76rfZ2T7Vt3h","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/sheet_index.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01W6TGPYqtUkp6jCAd2iZ9kc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/classification.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_013H7vcxBiqnuKmkwLKkGYpY","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/key_sheets.json"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":3,"output":331,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":12301,"totalTokens":12635,"cost":{"input":0.000015000000000000002,"output":0.008275000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.07688125,"total":0.08517125}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770062984305}}
{"type":"message","id":"e6be86cd","parentId":"9a25b245","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:09:49.669Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01YJcApHPzjiE6fsVgXufQSP","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# BluePrint — Construction Document Intelligence Engine\n\n> Chat-based preconstruction intelligence engine that reads a full project set like an expert estimator.\n\n## Purpose\n\nBluePrint ingests complete construction document sets (drawings + specifications), builds a structured understanding of the entire project, and provides scope intelligence for pricing. It thinks like a builder: demo first → room-by-room → cross-reference everything → flag the gotchas → quantify.\n\n**Completeness is the mission.** Missing scope/quantities is the #1 risk. BluePrint's primary job is making sure nothing slips through.\n\n## Core Rule\n\n> **Flag, don't assume.** If it's not on the drawings, flag it — never silently include inferred scope.\n\n## Triggers\n\nActivate BluePrint when the user:\n- Uploads construction drawings (PDF sets)\n- Uploads specifications (CSI-format PDFs)\n- Asks about project scope, finishes, partitions, quantities, takeoffs\n- Requests CSI division summaries, RFQ packages, or scope reports\n- Asks construction Q&A questions about a loaded project\n- Uses keywords: blueprint, plan review, scope, takeoff, RFQ, CSI, finish schedule, partition, demo\n\n## Trade Configuration\n\nBluePrint reads the **entire project** across all CSI divisions. Trade profiles control what gets full analysis vs. coordination-only flagging.\n\n### Trade Profiles\n\n| Profile | Focus Divisions | Use Case |\n|---------|----------------|----------|\n| Interior GC (default) | Demo, Concrete/Masonry, Rough Carpentry, Finish Carpentry, Painting, Flooring/Tiling + flex (Drywall, Doors, Specialties) | Doug's default |\n| Full GC | All CSI divisions | Full general contractor |\n| MEP | Div 21-28 | Mechanical/Electrical/Plumbing |\n| Custom | User-defined | Any trade combination |\n\n### Focus vs. Coordination\n- **Focus trades**: Full scope analysis, quantities, pricing intelligence, RFQ generation\n- **Coordination-only trades**: Flag for coordination impacts (e.g., \"mechanical diffuser in ceiling — confirm ceiling grid coordination\")\n\nSwitching trade profile re-filters existing analysis — no reprocessing required.\n\n### 6 Core Trades (Default Interior GC)\n1. **Demolition** — Existing conditions removal\n2. **Concrete/Masonry** — Structural/architectural concrete and masonry\n3. **Rough Carpentry** — Framing, blocking, backing\n4. **Finish Carpentry** — Millwork, trim, casework\n5. **Painting** — All paint/coating scopes\n6. **Flooring/Tiling** — All floor and wall tile/flooring scopes\n\n### Flex Trades (Configurable per project)\n- Drywall (Div 09 21 16)\n- Doors/Frames/Hardware (Div 08)\n- Specialties (Div 10)\n- Others as needed\n\n## Two-Pass Processing Pipeline\n\nSee `references/processing-pipeline.md` for full detail.\n\n### Overview\n```\nINTAKE → PASS 1 (Page-by-Page) → PASS 2 (Room-by-Room) → Q&A READY\n```\n\n- **Intake**: Upload PDF set → split, classify, OCR\n- **Pass 1**: Page-by-page ingestion — catalog every sheet, extract all data, parse all schedules, map cross-references\n- **Pass 2**: Room-by-room synthesis — build room inventory, apply finishes/partitions/doors, categorize scope by trade, generate flags\n- **Q&A Ready**: Conversational interface active\n\nProcessing time: **Overnight is acceptable** for a 30-sheet set. Thoroughness > speed.\n\n## Data Model\n\nSee `references/data-model.md` for full schema.\n\n### Key Entities\n- **Project** → Floors → Rooms (atomic unit)\n- **Room**: Floor → Room Name → Room Number (hierarchy)\n- **Partitions**: Shared objects between rooms — two faces, each side has its own finish belonging to the room it faces\n- **Demo Items**: Separate section (not nested under rooms)\n- **Schedules**: Finish, Door, Hardware, Equipment, Responsibility Matrix\n- **Flags**: Considerations, inferences, coordination items, conflicts, orphans\n\n## Flag Types\n\nBluePrint generates 8 types of flags:\n\n| Flag Type | Description | Example |\n|-----------|-------------|---------|\n| **Inferred Scope** | Work implied but not drawn | \"Epoxy demo → heavy floor prep likely needed\" |\n| **Coordination Impact** | Other-trade work affecting focus trades | \"Mechanical diffuser — confirm ceiling grid\" |\n| **Owner-Furnished** | OFI/OFCI items to exclude from pricing | \"Owner-furnished appliances per responsibility matrix\" |\n| **Atypical Condition** | Unusual detail worth noting | \"Existing window AC removal — investigate infill\" |\n| **Conflict** | Drawing vs. spec disagreement | \"Plan shows FT-1 in Room 101, finish schedule shows FT-2\" |\n| **Orphan Reference** | Callout to nonexistent detail/sheet | \"Detail 4/A3.2 called out but sheet A3.2 not in set\" |\n| **Missing Information** | Expected data not found | \"Room 105 not on finish schedule\" |\n| **Exclusion Recommended** | Item to specifically exclude for risk mitigation | \"FT-3 in finish schedule but not found on any drawing\" |\n| **Access/Height Impact** | Scope item requires non-standard access method | \"Painting exposed structure at 21' AFF — lift/scaffold required\" |\n\n[86 more lines in file. Use offset=101 to continue]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770062989667}}
