{"type":"message","id":"6554e303","parentId":"57f65df3","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:12:56.868Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the correct mapping. Let me examine the actual key sheets with this corrected understanding. The image tool already returned some useful data. Let me now examine more sheets systematically."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014HcKp8n8Ncufme1AxJuCKq","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_012.png","prompt":"This is A-201 Building Elevations for Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition. Extract ALL: 1) Each elevation view name and what it shows, 2) Building heights, floor-to-floor dimensions, 3) ALL exterior material callouts (brick, metal panel, storefront glazing types), 4) Storefront/window sizes and locations, 5) Overall building width and height dimensions. Be extremely detailed about materials and dimensions."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01QUcB5GCurAiFs9ejNjjL6E","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_021.png","prompt":"This is the Reflected Ceiling Plan and Roof Plan A-501 for Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition. Extract ALL: 1) Roof plan dimensions and total roof area, 2) All roof drains shown and their locations, 3) Ceiling types for each room/area, 4) Ceiling heights, 5) Any roof equipment. Be thorough about roof drain count and roof dimensions."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01CyyfBbor9QE6rt7Vez2Y6o","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_013.png","prompt":"This is A-221 Building Section for Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition. Extract ALL dimensions, floor-to-floor heights, wall assemblies, roof structure information, and building cross-section details. What is the total building height? What are the slab elevations?"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":559,"cacheRead":57087,"cacheWrite":588,"totalTokens":58235,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.013975000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0285435,"cacheWrite":0.0036750000000000003,"total":0.046198499999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770063167541}}
{"type":"message","id":"573f11bd","parentId":"6554e303","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:13:10.723Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014HcKp8n8Ncufme1AxJuCKq","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# A-201 Building Elevations - Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n## Project Information\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue, ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Address:** 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects, 200 Madison Avenue, 14th Floor, New York, NY 10016\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n- **Issue:** Issued Solution for Bid\n- **Scale (all elevations):** 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n\n---\n\n## Elevation Views\n\n### 1. E8 - AMBULANCE BAY (Elevation E)\n- **Scale:** 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n- **Orientation:** Shows the ambulance bay exterior elevation\n- **Features:** Shows storefront glazing systems, brick walls (existing and new), ballistic glazing, and section references to A-124 and A-F03\n\n### 2. C8 - AMBULANCE BAY (Elevation B)\n- **Scale:** 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n- **Orientation:** Primary front-facing elevation of the ambulance bay\n- **Features:** Large \"EMERGENCY\" signage across storefront, multiple storefront bays, entry doors, canopy, and detailed dimensioning along the base\n\n### 3. A8 - VESTIBULE (Elevation A)\n- **Scale:** 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n- **Orientation:** Vestibule elevation\n- **Features:** Backboard, smaller storefront openings, brick walls, security features\n\n### 4. Elevation C (unlabeled/upper area)\n- Shows section cuts and references to details A-300, A-307, A-124, A-205\n\n---\n\n## Elevation Keynotes (ED Addition)\n\n| Key | Description |\n|-----|-------------|\n| **A1** | HID post glass in aluminum to match storefront. See struct dwgs for additional info. |\n| **A3** | Ballistic resistant indoor aluminum & glass storefront swing door, bronze built providing (USBR model, Lak"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_012.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063190707}}
{"type":"message","id":"26ca906b","parentId":"573f11bd","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:13:27.699Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01QUcB5GCurAiFs9ejNjjL6E","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# A-501 Reflected Ceiling Plan and Roof Plan - Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n## 1) Roof Plan Dimensions and Area\n\nFrom the **Emergency Entrance Canopy Roof Plan (Detail A8)** at 1/4\" = 1'-0\":\n- The canopy roof appears to be approximately **36'-0\" x 21'-0\"** based on visible dimensions\n- Keynote A6 references: \"AREA OF NEW MATERIAL (ROOFING TYPE 1, SEE DETAIL 5/A-501). CONTRACTOR TO PROVIDE NEW R-31 (5.5\" MIN THICKNESS) & NEW ROOF MEMBRANE SLOPED TO ROOF DRAIN\"\n- **Cricket/slope noted**: \"CRICKET 1/4\" PER FT. SLOPE (TYP.)\"\n\nThe main roof area dimensions are not fully legible but the canopy roof plan shows grid dimensions between gridlines A through F and numbered grids.\n\n## 2) Roof Drains\n\n- **Keynote A0**: \"EXISTING ROOF DRAIN AND OVERFLOW DRAIN REINSTALLED IN NEW ROOF\" - indicates existing drains being reused\n- **Keynote A4**: \"PROVIDE CRICKETS & ROOF DRAINS (4) UNLESS NOTED FOR DRAINAGE\"\n- **4 roof drains** are called for per keynote A4\n- Drains are sloped to via 1/4\" per ft. crickets (typical)\n- At least **one existing roof drain** is reinstalled per A0\n\n**Total: Minimum 4 new roof drains + reinstalled existing drain(s)**\n\n## 3) Ceiling Types (from Ceiling Finished Legend)\n\n| Symbol | Type |\n|---|---|\n| **C-1** | 2'x2' Ceiling Tile, Non-Correctional Grade (Clean) |\n| **C-1.S** | 2'x2' Correctional Grade Ceiling (Secure) |\n\n**Security notes:**\n- All **patient access areas** must use correctional-grade secure ceiling unless otherwise noted\n- All patient light fixtures must use correctional-grade secure ceiling per installation requirements\n\nAreas shown on the **Level"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_021.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063207692}}
{"type":"message","id":"7f02839f","parentId":"26ca906b","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:13:41.490Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01CyyfBbor9QE6rt7Vez2Y6o","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# A-221 Building Section - Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n## Slab Elevations\n\n- **Ground Floor**: 13'-1 1/2\"\n- **Canopy T.O.S. (Top of Steel)**: 26'-7 1/2\"\n\n## Floor-to-Floor Heights\n\n- Ground Floor to Canopy T.O.S.: approximately 13'-6\" (26'-7 1/2\" minus 13'-1 1/2\")\n\n## Total Building Height\n\nThe canopy T.O.S. at **26'-7 1/2\"** represents the top of the structure. The ground floor elevation is **13'-1 1/2\"**, giving a single-story structure height of approximately **13'-6\"** above ground floor level.\n\n## Sections Shown\n\n1. **E7 - Cart Wash and Canopy Section** (1/4\" = 1'-0\") - Grid lines 5.B through 1.B\n2. **C7 - Emergency Department Vestibule South Section** (1/4\" = 1'-0\") - Grid lines A.B through 1.B\n3. **A7 - Ambulance Bay Section** (1/4\" = 1'-0\") - Grid lines A.B through C.B\n4. **A2 - Cart Wash and Security Area Section** (1/4\" = 1'-0\") - Grid lines A.B through C.B\n\n## Wall Assemblies & Construction Details\n\n- **2\" high poured concrete (CMC) wall base**\n- **New wall with continuous & blanket insulation** (visible in A2 section)\n- **Existing exterior uninsulated brick wall** (to remain)\n- **Existing poured concrete wall foundation**\n- **Existing exterior concrete sidewalk**\n- **New brick wall to match existing brick color/coursing** (keynote A2)\n- **Ballistic resistant exterior aluminum & glass storefront** (swing doors and sliding glass doors - keynotes A1, A3, A6, A8, A8.1)\n- **Bullet proofing** (1 RPT model) on various glazing assemblies\n\n## Roof"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_013.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063221483}}
{"type":"message","id":"9bf5863c","parentId":"7f02839f","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:13:48.037Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SquttsEViwVyWXg1yVpbdj","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_014.png","prompt":"This is A-223 Wall Section for Bellevue Hospital. Extract ALL wall assembly details: exterior wall compositions, insulation types and thicknesses, sheathing types, air barriers, waterproofing, and any dimensions. I need to understand the complete wall buildup for quantity takeoff."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01QaqSkPAnry4Pt7VC7RRHMs","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_018.png","prompt":"This is A-303 Roof Details for Bellevue Hospital. Extract ALL roof assembly details, roofing membrane types, insulation, and any dimensions. What is the complete roof buildup?"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_017bvp8vw31fPU6Yn51bSH7X","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_026.png","prompt":"This is the demolition plan AD-101 for Bellevue Hospital. Extract the scope of demolition work - what is being demolished, wall removals, door removals, and any areas called out for demolition."}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":418,"cacheRead":57675,"cacheWrite":2175,"totalTokens":60269,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.010450000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0288375,"cacheWrite":0.01359375,"total":0.05288625}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770063221490}}
{"type":"message","id":"d7f5d66e","parentId":"9bf5863c","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:02.901Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01SquttsEViwVyWXg1yVpbdj","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# A-223 Wall Section Analysis - Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n## Overview\n\nThis sheet contains **five exterior wall sections at Brick/CMU wall conditions**, all at 1\" = 1'-0\" scale:\n\n- **A8** - Exterior Wall Section @ Brick/CMU Wall (Grid 8)\n- **A6** - Exterior Wall Section @ Brick/CMU Wall (Grid 6)\n- **A5** - Exterior Wall Section @ Brick/CMU Wall (Grid 5)\n- **A3** - Exterior Wall Section @ Brick/CMU Wall (Grid 3)\n- **A1** - Exterior Wall Section @ Brick/CMU Wall (Grid 1)\n\n---\n\n## Wall Assembly Buildup (Exterior to Interior)\n\nBased on the section details visible, the typical **Brick/CMU exterior wall** assembly consists of:\n\n1. **Exterior Brick Veneer** - Face brick wythe (visible as hatched outer layer)\n2. **Air Cavity/Drainage Space** - Between brick and backup wall\n3. **CMU Backup Wall** - Concrete masonry units (visible as block pattern in sections)\n\n## Key Dimensions\n\n- **Ground Floor (Actual 1st Floor) Height**: 13'-1 1/2\" (noted at multiple sections)\n- **Canopy T.O.S. (Top of Steel)**: 28'-7 1/2\" (noted consistently across sections A8, A6, A5, A3, A1)\n\n## Structural & Related Elements\n\n- **Existing Roof Deck** - noted at top of sections\n- **Existing Canopy Ceiling Metal Panels** - at canopy soffit level\n- **Steel Beam** - \"See Struct Dwgs\" (at approximately Level C)\n- **Concrete Foundation Wall** - \"See Struct Drawing\" (at base)\n- **New Slab on Grade** - \"See Struct Dwgs\" (at ground floor)\n- **Exterior Sidewalk** - \"See Civil Dwgs\" (at grade, sections A3 and A1)\n- **Existing Exterior Terrace/Sidewalk** (at section"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_014.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063242871}}
{"type":"message","id":"1336cbb6","parentId":"d7f5d66e","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:17.972Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01QaqSkPAnry4Pt7VC7RRHMs","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# A-303.00 Roof Details — Bellevue Hospital (ED Ambulance Bay Addition)\n\n## Detail Inventory\n\n| Detail | Title | Scale |\n|--------|-------|-------|\n| **D8** | Emergency Entrance Canopy @ Brick Wall | 1½\" = 1'-0\" |\n| **D5** | Emergency Entrance Canopy @ Structural Support | 3\" = 1'-0\" |\n| **D2** | Emergency Entrance Canopy @ Skylight End Side | 3\" = 1'-0\" |\n| **A8** | Emergency Entrance Canopy @ Exp. Jt | 3\" = 1'-0\" |\n| **A6** | Emergency Entrance Canopy @ Perimeter Fascia | 3\" = 1'-0\" |\n| **A4** | Emergency Entrance Canopy @ Roof Drain | 3\" = 1'-0\" |\n\n## Roof Assembly / Buildup (Roof Type 1)\n\nFrom top to bottom, as extracted from the details:\n\n1. **Roofing membrane** (new roof membrane) — likely single-ply\n2. **Insulation** (sloped insulation / tapered insulation for drainage)\n3. **Existing metal deck** (existing 2\" metal deck noted to remain)\n\n## Key Components & Annotations\n\n- **Sealant tip** at EL. varies\n- **Flash-up all sides of opening a minimum of 8\" above roof level**\n- **Existing cont. metal flashing**\n- **T.O. Skylight Curb: EL. 30'-6\"**\n- **Canopy T.O.S.: 28'-7½\"**\n- **T.O.S. Canopy: EL. 28'-6\"** (multiple locations)\n- **Existing concrete curb**\n- **Existing halted translucent polycarbonate barrel/panel skylight system** (to remain)\n\n## Membrane & Flashing Details\n\n- **New roof membrane** — contractor to bring up roof flashing and install new roof membrane under/over coping and over flashing down to completion of metal curb"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_018.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063257965}}
{"type":"message","id":"21c0a926","parentId":"1336cbb6","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:24.953Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_017bvp8vw31fPU6Yn51bSH7X","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This image shows a **COMcheck Envelope Compliance Certificate and Inspection Checklist** for the **H+H Bellevue Hospital ED Ambulance Bay Addition** project, not a demolition plan AD-101. \n\nThe documents visible are energy code compliance forms, not demolition drawings. They detail:\n\n- Envelope assemblies (roofs, walls, doors, windows)\n- Energy conservation code compliance\n- Inspection checklists\n\n**No demolition scope, wall removals, door removals, or demolition areas are shown in this document.** This appears to be a COMcheck energy compliance submittal, not an architectural demolition plan. The actual demolition plan AD-101 would be a different sheet in the drawing set."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_026.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063264943}}
