{"type":"message","id":"56e660b8","parentId":"c26d0949","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:39.053Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01L691uVEgjhdM6SLXwm4U2d","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"project\": \"HHC Bellevue Hospital - Ambulance Drop Off Renovation\",\n  \"project_number\": \"11202402\",\n  \"takeoff_batch\": \"BATCH 1 - ARCHITECTURAL\",\n  \"extraction_date\": \"2026-02-02\",\n  \"prepared_by\": \"Clawdbot Quantity Surveyor\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"08-01_metal_doors_and_frames\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"08-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Metal Doors and Frames (Hollow Metal)\",\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Count from Door Schedule A-701\",\n        \"doors_included\": [\n          {\n            \"door_no\": \"ED-1-01\",\n            \"location\": \"CART WASH\",\n            \"size\": \"5'-0\\\" x 7'-0\\\"\",\n            \"material\": \"HM\",\n            \"frame\": \"HM 5'-4\\\" wide\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"door_no\": \"ED-1-09\",\n            \"location\": \"ENTRANCE VESTIBULE\",\n            \"size\": \"6'-0\\\" x 7'-0\\\" (PAIR)\",\n            \"material\": \"HM\",\n            \"frame\": \"HM 6'-4\\\" wide\",\n            \"notes\": \"Pair of doors, counted as 1 EA door assembly\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"ED-1-01 is single 5' wide HM door. ED-1-09 is a pair (6' total width) counted as one door assembly per schedule.\"\n    },\n    \"08-02_wood_doors\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"08-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Wood Doors\",\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 0,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Review of Door Schedule A-701\",\n        \"finding\": \"No wood doors specified in door schedule\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"All doors in this project are either Hollow Metal (HM) or Aluminum (AL). No wood doors required.\"\n    },\n    \"08-03_hardware\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"08-03\",\n      \"description\": \"Door Hardware\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Lump Sum based on 9 door assemblies with hardware sets\",\n        \"doors_requiring_hardware\": [\n          {\"door\": \"ED-1-01\", \"hardware_set\": \"1.0\"},\n          {\"door\": \"ED-1-02\", \"hardware_set\": \"3.0\"},\n          {\"door\": \"ED-1-03\", \"hardware_set\": \"5.0\"},\n          {\"door\": \"ED-1-04\", \"hardware_set\": \"6.0\"},\n          {\"door\": \"ED-1-06\", \"hardware_set\": \"3.0\"},\n          {\"door\": \"ED-1-07\", \"hardware_set\": \"3.0\"}\n        ],\n        \"special_hardware\": \"Ballistic-rated hardware for Level 3 doors\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"6 doors with assigned hardware sets per A-701. ED-1-08 and ED-1-09 have no hardware set shown (-). Includes closers, card readers, locks, hinges for HM and AL doors.\"\n    },\n    \"08-04_glass_and_glazing\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"08-04\",\n      \"description\": \"Glass and Glazing\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 375,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Sum of glazed areas from doors and storefronts\",\n        \"breakdown\": [\n          {\n            \"item\": \"ED-1-02 (Ballistic)\",\n            \"size\": \"3'-6 1/2\\\" x 7'-8\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 27\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"ED-1-03 (Ballistic)\",\n            \"size\": \"3'-0\\\" x 7'-8\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 23\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"ED-1-04 (Ballistic)\",\n            \"size\": \"3'-0\\\" x 7'-8\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 23\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"ED-1-06 Sliding Door (Ballistic)\",\n            \"size\": \"14'-4\\\" x 8'-0\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 115\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"ED-1-07 Sliding Door (Ballistic)\",\n            \"size\": \"14'-4\\\" x 8'-0\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 115\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"ED-1-08 (Ballistic)\",\n            \"size\": \"3'-6\\\" x 7'-8\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 27\n          },\n          {\n            \"item\": \"Storefront sidelites and transoms (estimated)\",\n            \"sf\": 45\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"All glazing is Ballistic Level 3 per spec 084113. Includes doors with BAL glazing and storefront glazing. Storefront glazing quantity estimated based on interior elevations showing extensive storefront at vestibule.\"\n    },\n    \"08-05_storefront_systems\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"08-05\",\n      \"description\": \"Storefront Systems\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 485,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Measured from A-101 plan and interior elevations\",\n        \"areas\": [\n          {\n            \"location\": \"Interior storefront at Vestibule (BES-05)\",\n            \"estimated_sf\": 240\n          },\n          {\n            \"location\": \"Exterior storefront at Vestibule/Entry\",\n            \"estimated_sf\": 180\n          },\n          {\n            \"location\": \"Security Station interior storefront\",\n            \"estimated_sf\": 65\n          }\n        ],\n        \"basis_of_design\": \"US Bullet Proofing (USBP) Model USAW400, Stanley Dura-Shield Security Series\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Ballistic-resistant aluminum storefront systems per A-200 and A-704 details. All storefront is thermally broken ballistic resistant type. Quantity estimated from plan measurements.\"\n    },\n    \"09-01_gypsum_wallboard\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"09-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Gypsum Wallboard\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 2850,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Wall perimeter x ceiling height minus openings, both sides of partitions\",\n        \"room_breakdown\": [\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART WASH\",\n            \"perimeter\": \"59 LF\",\n            \"height\": \"9'-0\\\"\",\n            \"gross_sf\": 531,\n            \"openings\": \"Door 35 SF\",\n            \"net_sf\": 496\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"SECURITY STATION\",\n            \"perimeter\": \"38 LF\",\n            \"height\": \"10'-0\\\"\",\n            \"gross_sf\": 380,\n            \"openings\": \"Doors/Storefront 120 SF\",\n            \"net_sf\": 260\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"NYPD SECURITY PICKUP\",\n            \"perimeter\": \"28 LF\",\n            \"height\": \"10'-0\\\"\",\n            \"gross_sf\": 280,\n            \"openings\": \"Doors 80 SF\",\n            \"net_sf\": 200\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"ENTRANCE VESTIBULE\",\n            \"perimeter\": \"60 LF\",\n            \"height\": \"10'-0\\\"\",\n            \"gross_sf\": 600,\n            \"openings\": \"Doors/Storefront 350 SF\",\n            \"net_sf\": 250\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART ALCOVE\",\n            \"perimeter\": \"26 LF\",\n            \"height\": \"9'-6\\\"\",\n            \"gross_sf\": 247,\n            \"openings\": \"0 SF\",\n            \"net_sf\": 247\n          }\n        ],\n        \"both_sides_multiplier\": 2,\n        \"total_net_wall_sf\": 1453,\n        \"ceiling_sf\": \"592 SF (C-2 ceilings only)\",\n        \"total_gyp_sf\": 2850\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"5/8\\\" Type X GWB per partition types. Includes walls on both sides of partitions and gypsum ceilings (C-2). Cart Wash has special coating on walls but GWB substrate. Excludes areas with porcelain tile, special wall coating, or plastic wall protection.\"\n    },\n    \"09-02_ceramic_tile\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"09-02\",\n      \"description\": \"Porcelain Tile (per finish schedule)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 145,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"From Finish Schedule A-801 - wall tile locations\",\n        \"locations\": [\n          {\n            \"location\": \"SECURITY STATION - North Wall (PT/W-1)\",\n            \"finish\": \"Silestone Cala Blue 2CM\",\n            \"sf\": 65,\n            \"notes\": \"Accent wall behind security desk\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"location\": \"SECURITY STATION - South Wall (PT/W-2)\",\n            \"finish\": \"Dekton Kreta 2CM\",\n            \"sf\": 80,\n            \"notes\": \"Security desk surround\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"wall_height_factor\": \"2CM thick porcelain tile, full height to ceiling (10'-0\\\")\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Finish schedule specifies PT/W-1 and PT/W-2 as 2CM porcelain tile walls, not ceramic tile. Quantity based on wall dimensions from A-101 plan. Metal trim MT-1 at tile corners.\"\n    },\n    \"09-03_acoustical_ceiling\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"09-03\",\n      \"description\": \"Acoustical Ceiling Tile\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 173,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Room floor areas for rooms with C-1 ceiling finish\",\n        \"rooms_with_act\": [\n          {\n            \"room\": \"SECURITY STATION\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"12'-8 1/4\\\" x 6'-6 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 82.4,\n            \"ceiling_type\": \"C-1 Armstrong Optima\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"NYPD SECURITY PICKUP\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"6'-3 1/4\\\" x 7'-11 1/2\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 49.8,\n            \"ceiling_type\": \"C-1 Armstrong Optima\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART ALCOVE\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"6'-6 1/4\\\" x 6'-3 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 40.8,\n            \"ceiling_type\": \"C-1 Armstrong Optima\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"total_act_sf\": 173,\n        \"ceiling_details\": \"Armstrong 3214 Optima Health Beveled Tegular 24\\\"x24\\\", Prelude 15/16\\\" grid\"\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"3 rooms with ACT (C-1) per finish schedule. CART WASH and ENTRANCE VESTIBULE have C-2 (gypsum) ceilings. Includes grid system. Security ceiling per spec for patient access areas.\"\n    },\n    \"09-04_resilient_flooring\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"09-04\",\n      \"description\": \"Poured Epoxy Flooring (per finish schedule)\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 592,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Sum of floor areas for all 5 rooms\",\n        \"room_breakdown\": [\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART WASH\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"16'-9 1/4\\\" x 12'-8 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 212.3,\n            \"finish\": \"PE-2 Stonclad-UR Pewter\",\n            \"base\": \"IEB-2 6\\\" integral epoxy base\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"SECURITY STATION\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"12'-8 1/4\\\" x 6'-6 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 82.4,\n            \"finish\": \"PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 White Ebony\",\n            \"base\": \"IEB-1 6\\\" integral epoxy base\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"NYPD SECURITY PICKUP\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"6'-3 1/4\\\" x 7'-11 1/2\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 49.8,\n            \"finish\": \"PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 White Ebony\",\n            \"base\": \"IEB-1 6\\\" integral epoxy base\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"ENTRANCE VESTIBULE\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"18'-9 1/4\\\" x 11'-0 1/2\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 206.9,\n            \"finish\": \"PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 White Ebony\",\n            \"base\": \"IEB-1 6\\\" integral epoxy base\",\n            \"notes\": \"Walk-off mat by H+H at entrance\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART ALCOVE\",\n            \"dimensions\": \"6'-6 1/4\\\" x 6'-3 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"sf\": 40.8,\n            \"finish\": \"PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 White Ebony\",\n            \"base\": \"IEB-1 6\\\" integral epoxy base\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"total_sf\": 592.2\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"All rooms receive poured epoxy flooring per A-801 finish schedule. PE-2 in Cart Wash (Stonclad-UR Pewter), PE-1 in other rooms (Stonres-RTZ-2 White Ebony). Includes 6\\\" integral epoxy base at all walls.\"\n    },\n    \"09-05_painting\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"09-05\",\n      \"description\": \"Painting\",\n      \"unit\": \"SF\",\n      \"quantity\": 2100,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Wall SF (perimeter x height) minus openings and areas with other finishes\",\n        \"room_breakdown\": [\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART WASH\",\n            \"wall_sf\": 531,\n            \"deductions\": \"Special coating SWC-1 all walls (531 SF)\",\n            \"paint_sf\": 0,\n            \"ceiling_paint\": \"P-3 epoxy on C-2 ceiling (212 SF)\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"SECURITY STATION\",\n            \"wall_sf\": 380,\n            \"deductions\": \"PT/W-1 (65 SF), PT/W-2 (80 SF), Storefront (~60 SF)\",\n            \"paint_sf\": 175,\n            \"paint_spec\": \"P-1 Benjamin Moore Epoxy Mountain Peak White\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"NYPD SECURITY PICKUP\",\n            \"wall_sf\": 280,\n            \"deductions\": \"Doors (~50 SF)\",\n            \"paint_sf\": 230,\n            \"paint_spec\": \"P-1 Benjamin Moore Epoxy\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"ENTRANCE VESTIBULE\",\n            \"wall_sf\": 600,\n            \"deductions\": \"Storefront/doors (~180 SF)\",\n            \"paint_sf\": 420,\n            \"paint_spec\": \"P-1 Benjamin Moore Epoxy\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"room\": \"CART ALCOVE\",\n            \"wall_sf\": 247,\n            \"deductions\": \"PWP-1 wall protection north/south (~65 SF)\",\n            \"paint_sf\": 182,\n            \"paint_spec\": \"P-1 Benjamin Moore Epoxy\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"wall_paint_subtotal\": 1007,\n        \"ceiling_paint_c2\": 419,\n        \"total_paint_sf\": 2100\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"P-1 Benjamin Moore Epoxy on walls. P-2 Flat on C-2 gypsum ceilings. Cart Wash walls receive SWC-1 special coating (Stonglaze VSR Ash Grey) not paint. Excludes areas with tile, wall protection, or storefront.\"\n    },\n    \"09-06_wall_protection\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"09-06\",\n      \"description\": \"Wall Protection\",\n      \"unit\": \"LF\",\n      \"quantity\": 22,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Linear feet of PWP-1 at specified height\",\n        \"location\": \"CART ALCOVE - North and South walls\",\n        \"details\": [\n          {\n            \"wall\": \"North wall\",\n            \"length\": \"6'-3 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"height\": \"60\\\" (5'-0\\\")\",\n            \"finish\": \"PWP-1 INPRO Palladium White Sand\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"wall\": \"South wall\",\n            \"length\": \"6'-3 1/4\\\"\",\n            \"height\": \"60\\\" (5'-0\\\")\",\n            \"finish\": \"PWP-1 INPRO Palladium White Sand\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"corner_guard\": \"CG-1 at corner\",\n            \"location\": \"Cart Alcove\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"linear_feet\": 12.5,\n        \"linear_feet_both_walls\": 22\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"PWP-1 INPRO Palladium White Sand 60\\\" high on north and south walls of Cart Alcove per A-801. Corner guard CG-1 also required. Quantified as LF of wall protection installed.\"\n    },\n    \"12-01_casework\": {\n      \"item_code\": \"12-01\",\n      \"description\": \"Casework\",\n      \"unit\": \"LF\",\n      \"quantity\": 28,\n      \"calculation\": {\n        \"method\": \"Linear feet from interior elevations and equipment plan\",\n        \"locations\": [\n          {\n            \"location\": \"SECURITY STATION - Main counter\",\n            \"elevation\": \"A-400 elevations A8, A6, 10, 11, 12\",\n            \"estimated_lf\": 18,\n            \"details\": \"Security desk with transaction counter, pass-through\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"location\": \"SECURITY STATION - Additional cabinets\",\n            \"estimated_lf\": 6,\n            \"details\": \"Wall cabinets and storage\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"location\": \"CART WASH - Casework\",\n            \"estimated_lf\": 4,\n            \"notes\": \"Minimal casework in cart wash area\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"total_linear_feet\": 28\n      },\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Casework details referenced on A-702 but dimensions not fully shown. Security control desk with phenolic panels and solid surface countertops per A-702 details. Includes base cabinets, wall cabinets, and countertops. Quantity estimated from interior elevations - requires field verification or shop drawing confirmation.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total_items\": 12,\n    \"high_confidence\": 7,\n    \"medium_confidence\": 4,\n    \"low_confidence\": 1\n  },\n  \"data_sources\": [\n    \"A-101 Construction Plan (page_009)\",\n    \"A-501 Reflected Ceiling Plan (page_021)\",\n    \"A-701 Door Schedule (synthesis/door_schedule_complete.json)\",\n    \"A-702 Casework and Interior Details (page_023)\",\n    \"A-801 Finish Schedule (synthesis/finish_schedule_complete.json)\",\n    \"A-400 Interior Elevations (page_020)\"\n  ],\n  \"key_assumptions\": [\n    \"Room dimensions measured from A-101 Construction Plan at 1/4\\\" = 1'-0\\\" scale\",\n    \"Ceiling heights from finish schedule and RCP\",\n    \"Door quantities from Door Schedule A-701 (9 doors total, 1 appears to be missing ED-1-05)\",\n    \"Casework quantities estimated from interior elevations - limited dimensional data available\",\n    \"Storefront and glazing quantities estimated from plan and elevation views\",\n    \"Wall protection linear footage based on finish schedule showing PWP-1 on Cart Alcove walls\"\n  ]\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063279051}}
{"type":"message","id":"af32891b","parentId":"56e660b8","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:39.055Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01LwPAjRicvAFdgRfnhcSDn8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"project\": \"HHC Bellevue Hospital - Ambulance Drop Off Renovation\",\n  \"project_number\": \"11202402\",\n  \"takeoff_batch\": \"BATCH 2 - STRUCTURAL, CIVIL & SITE\",\n  \"extraction_date\": \"2026-02-02\",\n  \"items\": {\n    \"03-01_concrete_foundations\": {\"item_code\": \"03-01\", \"description\": \"Concrete Foundations (Pile Caps, Grade Beams, Slab)\", \"unit\": \"CY\", \"quantity\": 42.5, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"4 pile caps (~12 CY), GB-1 (2.7 CY), GB-2 (4.2 CY), SOG (21.9 CY), DB-1 (0.7 CY). 4000 PSI, Grade 60 rebar.\"},\n    \"03-02_concrete_slab_on_grade\": {\"item_code\": \"03-02\", \"description\": \"Concrete Slab on Grade\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 592, \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"notes\": \"12\\\" thick, #6@12\\\" OC double mat. 5 rooms total from A-101.\"},\n    \"03-03_concrete_paving\": {\"item_code\": \"03-03\", \"description\": \"Concrete Paving (Site)\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 385, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Curb/gutter (180 SF), walks (145 SF), misc (60 SF). Verify with civil drawings.\"},\n    \"04-01_unit_masonry\": {\"item_code\": \"04-01\", \"description\": \"Unit Masonry (Brick/CMU)\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 485, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"BES-05 brick on CFMF (280 SF), BES-10 brick on CMU (145 SF), BES-11 insulated existing (60 SF). Match existing.\"},\n    \"05-01_structural_steel\": {\"item_code\": \"05-01\", \"description\": \"Structural Steel Framing\", \"unit\": \"LB\", \"quantity\": 8750, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"From S-101. W8x35 beams, W8x24 secondary, HSS6x6x5/8 posts, channels, angles. Top of steel 27'-2\\\". A992/A572 Gr50.\"},\n    \"05-02_metal_canopy\": {\"item_code\": \"05-02\", \"description\": \"Metal Canopy\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"~37'x18' = 485 SF. Steel frame + metal deck + PMMA roofing + fascia/soffit (78 LF) + gutters (42 LF). Connects to existing W27x84/W27x146.\"},\n    \"05-03_misc_metal\": {\"item_code\": \"05-03\", \"description\": \"Miscellaneous Metal\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"Shelf angles (145 LF), lintels (6 EA), HSS posts for storefront (4 EA), bollards (6 EA), flood barrier system (1 EA).\"},\n    \"06-01_rough_carpentry\": {\"item_code\": \"06-01\", \"description\": \"Rough Carpentry\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"~200 BF FR treated lumber. Blocking for storefront, equipment, casework. Most framing is CFMF.\"},\n    \"07-01_waterproofing\": {\"item_code\": \"07-01\", \"description\": \"Waterproofing\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 925, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"SOG membrane (592 SF), foundation wall (285 SF), air/water barrier on walls (485 SF). Some overlap with insulation.\"},\n    \"07-02_building_insulation\": {\"item_code\": \"07-02\", \"description\": \"Building Insulation\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 1680, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"2\\\" polyiso R-8.5 walls (485 SF), 3.5\\\" batt R-13 (485 SF), R-15 slab edge (195 SF), R-7.5 foundation (145 SF), R-33 roof (485 SF), flute fill (85 SF).\"},\n    \"07-03_roofing\": {\"item_code\": \"07-03\", \"description\": \"Roofing (PMMA)\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 485, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"Canopy roof only. PMMA liquid applied + cover board + R-33 polyiso. 1/4\\\"/ft slope to drains.\"},\n    \"07-04_firestopping\": {\"item_code\": \"07-04\", \"description\": \"Firestopping\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"All MEP penetrations through rated walls, roof, slab. Hospital occupancy = strict compliance.\"},\n    \"07-05_joint_sealants\": {\"item_code\": \"07-05\", \"description\": \"Joint Sealants\", \"unit\": \"LF\", \"quantity\": 485, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"Storefront perimeters (165 LF), door frames (95 LF), control joints (125 LF), expansion joints (65 LF), roof joints (35 LF).\"},\n    \"31-01_site_excavation\": {\"item_code\": \"31-01\", \"description\": \"Site Excavation\", \"unit\": \"CY\", \"quantity\": 95, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Foundation excavation (54 CY) + general site (46 CY) adjusted for shrinkage. Dewatering required per FO-002.\"},\n    \"31-02_site_fill\": {\"item_code\": \"31-02\", \"description\": \"Site Fill/Grading\", \"unit\": \"CY\", \"quantity\": 65, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Structural backfill (45 CY) + site grading (20 CY). 95% compaction required.\"},\n    \"32-01_asphalt_paving\": {\"item_code\": \"32-01\", \"description\": \"Asphalt Paving\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 1850, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Ambulance court (1250 SF), new ramp (385 SF), repairs (215 SF). 3\\\" binder + 2\\\" wearing. Verify with civil.\"},\n    \"32-02_site_concrete\": {\"item_code\": \"32-02\", \"description\": \"Site Concrete\", \"unit\": \"SF\", \"quantity\": 650, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Curbs (145 SF), walks (385 SF), bollard foundations (24 SF), canopy piers (96 SF).\"},\n    \"32-03_site_utilities\": {\"item_code\": \"32-03\", \"description\": \"Site Utilities\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Storm, sanitary, water, possibly gas connections. Minimal new piping for this addition.\"},\n    \"32-04_erosion_control\": {\"item_code\": \"32-04\", \"description\": \"Erosion Control\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"Silt fence (185 LF), inlet protection (4 EA), construction entrance, dust control. NYC DEP/NYSDEC compliance.\"},\n    \"33-01_storm_drainage\": {\"item_code\": \"33-01\", \"description\": \"Storm Drainage\", \"unit\": \"LF\", \"quantity\": 145, \"confidence\": \"LOW\", \"notes\": \"Roof drain leaders (65 LF), site storm piping (55 LF), area drains (3 EA). Verify with C-102.\"},\n    \"33-02_site_electrical\": {\"item_code\": \"33-02\", \"description\": \"Site Electrical\", \"unit\": \"LS\", \"quantity\": 1, \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"notes\": \"Exterior/security lighting, camera power, underground conduit (125 LF), HandWave plates (4 EA).\"}\n  },\n  \"summary\": {\"total_items\": 21, \"high_confidence\": 1, \"medium_confidence\": 12, \"low_confidence\": 8},\n  \"data_sources\": [\"FO-101/FO-200/FO-201/FO-300 Foundation Plans\", \"S-101 Canopy Framing Plan\", \"A-101/A-200/A-221/A-223/A-224/A-301/A-303/A-501\", \"BES Wall Type Details\"],\n  \"key_assumptions\": [\n    \"Foundation volumes from FO-101 plan and FO-300 sections\",\n    \"Structural steel from S-101 with standard AISC weights\",\n    \"Canopy area ~37'x18' = 485 SF from grid spacing\",\n    \"Masonry from BES-05/10/11 wall types and elevation views\",\n    \"Site work quantities LOW confidence - civil drawings partially available\",\n    \"Asphalt paving estimated from demo plan notation referencing civil drawings\"\n  ]\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063279054}}
{"type":"message","id":"ba2f5001","parentId":"af32891b","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:39.058Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01GsCXAQ3Do2BwxzgSA6DXcK","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"project\": \"HHC Bellevue Hospital - Ambulance Drop Off Renovation\",\n  \"project_number\": \"11202402\",\n  \"batch\": \"Batch 3 - MEP, Specialties & General\",\n  \"extraction_date\": \"2026-02-02\",\n  \"takeoff_items\": [\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"02-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Existing Conditions\",\n      \"description\": \"Asbestos Abatement\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Complete asbestos abatement of identified ACM materials per environmental survey prior to any demolition work. Includes abatement of existing materials in ambulance drop-off area, coordination with Owner's environmental consultant, containment barriers, negative air systems, air monitoring, and proper disposal per NYC DEP requirements. Spec section 028200 applies. Work must be completed BEFORE any construction demolition begins per ICRA requirements.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on hazmat drawings H-001 and H-101. Abatement area covers existing ambulance bay renovation footprint including ceiling systems, wall materials, and flooring with ACM content.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Exact ACM quantities require field survey verification. Environmental Planning Management is the environmental engineer. Coordination with hospital infection control is critical. ILSM and ICM measures required during abatement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"02-02\",\n      \"category\": \"Existing Conditions\",\n      \"description\": \"Selective Demolition - Interior\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Selective demolition of existing ambulance drop-off area including: removal of existing exterior wall sections at ambulance bay; removal of existing entrance doors and frames; removal of existing ceiling systems in affected areas (including grid, tiles, lighting, diffusers); removal of existing floor finishes down to concrete slab; removal of existing partitions as indicated on AD-101; removal of existing medical equipment and fixed equipment; removal of weathering steel cladding for reuse. Includes protection of adjacent occupied areas, dust containment, and disposal.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum scope based on demolition plan AD-101. Area approximately 3,200 SF per code summary. Includes coordination with structural engineer for bracing during demolition.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"Contractor must field verify existing conditions. Hazardous material abatement must precede demolition. Existing recreation deck above to remain. Weathering steel panels to be removed carefully for reuse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"02-03\",\n      \"category\": \"Existing Conditions\",\n      \"description\": \"Site Demolition\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Site demolition includes: saw-cut and remove existing asphalt pavement at canopy foundation locations (approximate scope shown on AD-101); remove existing curbing as indicated; remove existing bollards (D6/D7 locations); remove existing siamese connection (D4); remove existing hose bibb (D5); demolish existing concrete slab where indicated; remove iron fence and curb. Includes saw-cutting, excavation for new foundations, and proper disposal.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on civil/site drawings C-050 and AD-101 demolition plan. Coordinate with canopy foundation locations on S-101.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Exact pavement removal quantities depend on final canopy foundation layout. Contractor to coordinate exact scope with new work. See civil drawings for additional site demo scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"10-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Specialties\",\n      \"description\": \"Visual Display Boards\",\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 2,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Visual display boards/monitors for security station. Located at Security room and NYPD Security Pickup area. Owner-furnished equipment with contractor providing power, data connections, and mounting infrastructure.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Count from A-101 equipment plan and A-801 furniture plan. 1 display at Security desk, 1 at NYPD pickup area.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Verify exact quantities with Owner's security consultant MG Engineering. Equipment likely owner-furnished/contractor-installed (OFCI).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"10-02\",\n      \"category\": \"Specialties\",\n      \"description\": \"Signage\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Interior and exterior signage including: illuminated 'EMERGENCY' signage above entrance (new); room identification signs; exit signs (coordinate with E-201); fire extinguisher cabinet signage; security area signage; wayfinding/directional signage as required by code. Includes all mounting hardware and electrical connections for illuminated signs.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on signage indicated on A-101, E-201, and code requirements. Key illuminated sign above entrance vestibule noted on reflected ceiling plan.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Coordinate signage with Owner's standards. NYC Health + Hospitals may have specific signage requirements. ADA compliant signage required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"10-03\",\n      \"category\": \"Specialties\",\n      \"description\": \"Toilet Compartments\",\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 0,\n      \"scope_description\": \"No new toilet compartments in new construction scope. This is an ambulance bay entrance/security area without toilet rooms. Existing toilet compartments to be demolished (see 02-02).\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Reviewed A-101 construction plan, A-701 partition schedule, and P-101 plumbing plan. No toilet rooms in new addition.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"Demolition scope includes removal of approximately 4-6 existing toilet compartments in affected areas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"10-04\",\n      \"category\": \"Specialties\",\n      \"description\": \"Toilet Accessories\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Toilet accessories package for any remaining/restroom areas affected by renovation. Includes toilet paper dispensers, paper towel dispensers, soap dispensers, mirrors, grab bars as required, and related accessories. Coordinate with any existing restrooms that remain operational.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Minimal scope - verify if any existing restrooms remain in adjacent areas requiring accessory upgrades.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"notes\": \"Primary scope is demolition of existing toilet rooms. Verify with Owner if any accessory upgrades required in adjacent remaining facilities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"10-05\",\n      \"category\": \"Specialties\",\n      \"description\": \"Fire Extinguishers\",\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 4,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Fire extinguisher cabinets and extinguishers. Located per code requirements throughout new construction area. Wall-mounted cabinets with proper signage. Type and size per code and FDNY requirements.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Count based on travel distance requirements per code (max 100 ft to extinguisher) and floor plan layout. Approximately 4 locations: Security area, Vestibule area, Cart Wash, and Corridor.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Fire extinguisher symbol (FEC/FE) shown in legend. Exact locations to be coordinated with Architect and FDNY. Cabinets to match Owner's standards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"11-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Equipment\",\n      \"description\": \"Security Equipment\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Security equipment package including: security station equipment (consoles, workstations, monitors); card reader access control systems; door position switches; motion sensors at entrance; intercom systems; security cameras (360 cameras indicated at entrance vestibule - 2 locations); camera mounting hardware; associated power supplies and low voltage cabling. Integration with existing hospital security system.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on A-101, E-101, and security consultant (MG Engineering) requirements. 2-3 cameras visible on plans plus security station infrastructure.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Security design by MG Engineering D.P.C. Coordinate with Owner's security department. Some equipment may be Owner-furnished. Weapon detection system is separate line item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"11-02\",\n      \"category\": \"Equipment\",\n      \"description\": \"Weapon Detection System\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Weapon detection system at main entrance vestibule. Includes detection equipment, pedestals, hand-wave plates, control units, power connections (dedicated circuits per E-101), integration with security system. Located at Entrance Vestibule for ambulance bay access screening. Includes 30\\\"x48\\\" clearance for wheelchair accessibility per plan.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum system shown on A-101 and E-101. One complete weapon detection station at primary entrance.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"Critical security component for hospital entrance. Verify exact system requirements with MG Engineering and Owner. Dedicated electrical circuits required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"11-03\",\n      \"category\": \"Equipment\",\n      \"description\": \"Medical Equipment\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Minor medical equipment package for ambulance drop-off area. This is not a patient treatment area - it is an entrance/security zone. Equipment may include: backboard storage racks (shown on A-101 - 2 locations); cart storage equipment; decontamination-related equipment per 11-04. No major medical equipment like imaging or surgical equipment in this scope.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on equipment plan A-102 and Owner requirements. Backboard storage and cart storage are primary items.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"This is an ambulance entrance/security area, not a treatment area. Medical equipment scope is limited to storage and support functions. Verify with Owner for any specific equipment needs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"11-04\",\n      \"category\": \"Equipment\",\n      \"description\": \"Decontamination Equipment\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Decontamination equipment for ambulance bay area. Includes decontamination shower systems, eyewash stations, hose connections for wash-down. Located at 'Decontamination' areas shown on plans. Includes plumbing connections, drainage, and any specialty decon equipment per hospital requirements.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on 'Decontamination' areas shown on A-101 and plumbing plans. Includes hose bibbs and drainage at decon locations.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Coordinate exact decon requirements with hospital infection control and MG Engineering. Cart Wash area has special flooring and wall protection for wash-down operations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"13-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Special Construction\",\n      \"description\": \"Special Construction - Flood Barriers, Ballistic Panels\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Special construction assemblies including: Ballistic resistant panels (7/16\\\" fiberglass ballistic panels) at partitions Type 7D, 7E, and other security walls - installed from floor to 4\\\" above ceiling, continuous; Ballistic Level 3 glazing and frames at multiple doors (ED-1-02, ED-1-03, ED-1-04, ED-1-06, ED-1-07, ED-1-08) per door schedule; Flood-resistant construction at flood zone areas; Special security wall assemblies with batten seams per manufacturer requirements; Flood barriers or floodproofing measures as required for ambulance bay in flood zone.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Ballistic panels: approximately 200-300 SF of 7/16\\\" fiberglass panels based on partition types 7D/7E at security areas. 6 doors with ballistic Level 3 glazing per A-701 door schedule. Flood protection per G-004 flood map data and code requirements.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Ballistic panels on vestibule/public side of walls. Coordinate panel layout with stud spacing. Project is in flood zone per G-004 - verify if active flood barriers required or if static floodproofing is adequate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"14-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Conveying Equipment\",\n      \"description\": \"Conveying Equipment\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 0,\n      \"scope_description\": \"No conveying equipment (elevators, lifts, escalators) in this project scope. This is a single-story ambulance bay addition at ground level.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"N/A - single story addition.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"No vertical transportation required. Ramp provided for accessibility at entrance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"21-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Fire Suppression\",\n      \"description\": \"Fire Sprinkler System\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Fire sprinkler system modifications including: sprinkler head relocations for new ceiling layout; new sprinkler heads in new construction areas to provide NFPA 13 coverage; coordination with new canopy structure; connection to existing hospital wet pipe system; flow switches, valve assemblies, and trim; inspector's test assemblies; fire department connections (siamese connection replacement). Existing sprinklers to remain during early demo, with modifications as required.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on SP-101 sprinkler plan. Approximately 30-50 sprinkler heads in new/modified areas. Coverage for approximately 3,200 SF plus canopy area.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Sprinkler coverage must account for canopy structure per mep_coordination_review.json. ILSM required during modifications per spec 015010. Tie-in to existing hospital fire command center.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"22-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Plumbing\",\n      \"description\": \"Plumbing Piping\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Plumbing piping systems including: domestic water supply piping (cold and hot); sanitary waste and vent piping; storm drainage; floor drains (Cart Wash area); hose bibbs (exterior and Cart Wash); water supply for decontamination areas; connections to existing hospital systems. No med gas piping (not a treatment area). Acid-resistant drainage if required for decon chemicals.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on P-101 plumbing plan and P-100 underground plan. Coordinate with existing utilities. Includes riser connections per P-300.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Cart Wash drainage requires special consideration. Verify acid-resistant requirements with Owner. Underground work in P-100 scope. No medical gas - this is ambulance entrance not patient treatment area per mep_coordination_review.json.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"22-02\",\n      \"category\": \"Plumbing\",\n      \"description\": \"Plumbing Fixtures\",\n      \"unit\": \"EA\",\n      \"quantity\": 0,\n      \"scope_description\": \"No new plumbing fixtures (water closets, lavatories, sinks, drinking fountains) in new construction scope. This is an ambulance bay entrance/security area without toilet rooms. Floor drains only - see 22-01. Existing fixtures to be removed in demolition areas.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Reviewed A-101 construction plan and P-101 plumbing plan. No new toilet rooms or fixtures in addition.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"notes\": \"Demolition scope includes removal of existing plumbing fixtures in affected areas (estimated 4-6 water closets, 2-4 lavatories). Cart Wash area has floor drain but no plumbing fixtures per se.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"23-01\",\n      \"category\": \"HVAC\",\n      \"description\": \"HVAC Ductwork\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"HVAC ductwork for new ACU-1 air conditioning unit and ventilation system including: supply ductwork distribution; return air pathways; exhaust ductwork; fire and smoke dampers (UL labeled, gauge per schedule); volume control dampers; ductwork connections to diffusers and grilles; ductwork supports and hangers (black iron per code); ductwork insulation; coordination with structural steel canopy. Ductwork routing must clear structural steel for canopy per MEP conflict flag MEP-01.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on M-101 mechanical plan. Approximately 1,500-2,500 SF of ductwork surface area estimated for 3,200 SF space with 10' ceilings.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Ceiling heights 9'-0\\\" to 10'-0\\\" - verify duct clearance above ACT grid. Coordinate with canopy structure. ICRA negative pressure requirements during construction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"23-02\",\n      \"category\": \"HVAC\",\n      \"description\": \"HVAC Equipment\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"HVAC equipment including: ACU-1 new air conditioning unit (13kVA electrical load, 3-phase) serving ambulance bay area; existing exhaust fans (East/West) to remain with any needed modifications; cabinet unit heaters as indicated; air curtains at entrance (coordinate with spec); diffusers and grilles (linear diffusers, return grilles); louvers; fire/smoke dampers; ventilation panel VP-1; heating coils with 2-way valves; combination flow measuring/balancing valves. Equipment pads and supports.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on M-101, M-201 schedules, and mep_coordination_review.json. ACU-1 is primary new equipment. Existing exhaust fans to remain.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"ACU-1 routing must clear structural steel for canopy. Unit located on roof per plan. Verify capacity with cooling load calculations. Coordinate seismic requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"23-03\",\n      \"category\": \"HVAC\",\n      \"description\": \"Controls\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"HVAC control systems including: thermostats; occupancy sensors (ceiling mounted); CO2 sensors if required; control dampers; control valves (2-way hot water valves); DDC controllers for ACU-1 and unit heaters; integration with building automation system; control wiring and conduit. Coordinate with Division 25 Building Automation.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on M-401 through M-403 control drawings. Zone controls for ACU-1 and heating equipment.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Coordinate control sequences with Owner's standards. Integration with existing hospital BAS.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"25-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Integrated Automation\",\n      \"description\": \"Building Automation\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Building automation system integration for new HVAC equipment including: DDC controllers; field devices (sensors, actuators); control panels; integration with existing hospital BAS; programming and commissioning; graphics; alarms and trending. Integration with ACU-1, unit heaters, and associated equipment.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on control drawings M-401 through M-403. Integration points for ACU-1 and heating equipment.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Coordinate with hospital facilities for BAS integration protocol. Existing hospital may have specific BAS standards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"26-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Electrical\",\n      \"description\": \"Electrical Service\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Electrical service for new addition including: connection to existing panel CEHDP-A (480/277V, 3-phase, 2000A existing bus); new circuit for ACU-1 (3-#2 + 1#10G, 3/4\\\"C, 20A 3-pole breaker, 13kVA load per E-301); new distribution panels (LP-1, CDP-1, CDP-2, CDP-A, CDPE-1); feeders and conduits (2\\\"-10\\\" EMT noted); emergency power connections (Life Safety, Critical Branch, Equipment Branch); grounding systems; surge protection.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on E-101 power plan and E-301 panel schedules. Verify existing panel CEHDP-A capacity for new ACU-1 load.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"CEHDP-A has existing 2000A bus with options noted. Multiple emergency power branches require transfer switch coordination per MEP-03 conflict flag. 13kVA ACU-1 load is significant addition - verify capacity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"26-02\",\n      \"category\": \"Electrical\",\n      \"description\": \"Lighting\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Complete lighting system including: light fixtures per E-002 schedule (NF1, DNF1, DNF12, DNF13, LF2, LF-D, LF-A, DNF11 types); exit signs at all doorways (internally illuminated, LED, emergency powered); emergency lighting fixtures (DNF1(E) on emergency circuits); photocell sensors at exterior locations; occupancy sensors (ceiling mounted, single and two-zone); lighting controls and switching; fixture mounting hardware. All fixtures LED type per energy code.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Fixture counts from E-201 lighting plan: NF1 (~28), DNF1 (~9), DNF12 (~5), DNF13 (~4), LF2 (~7), LF-D (~5), LF-A (~4), DNF11 (~3), Exit Signs (~5), Emergency fixtures (~5). Total approximately 70-75 fixtures.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Note 17 on A-501 states 'Light fixture quantities to be confirmed by Contractor before pricing and ordering.' All fixtures to align with ceiling grid. Exit signs centered over doors per code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"26-03\",\n      \"category\": \"Electrical\",\n      \"description\": \"Power Distribution\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Power distribution including: new panels (LP-1, CDP-1, CDP-2, CDP-A, CDPE-1, FA-5-A, FA-5-B); panel schedules per E-301, E-302, E-303; branch circuit wiring; conduits (EMT, sizes 3/4\\\" to 2\\\" typical); outlets and receptacles (hospital grade per Note 9, emergency receptacles in red); dedicated circuits for ACU-1, weapon detection, sliding door operators; quadruplex outlets at equipment zones; isolated ground receptacles for equipment; fire-rated penetrations; access panels for panels in non-accessible ceilings.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on E-101 power plan. Approximately 30-40 receptacles/outlets. 6-8 new panels plus connections to existing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"All receptacles hospital grade. Emergency receptacles in red color. GFCI required at wet locations. Coordinate dedicated circuits with equipment requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"27-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Communications\",\n      \"description\": \"Data/Telecom\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Data and telecommunications systems including: voice/data outlets; access points (2 shown on E-201 reflected ceiling plan); cabling infrastructure (CAT6A or higher); cable trays or J-hooks; racks and patch panels; MDF/IDF connections; grounding; testing and certification. Security system cabling separate under 11-01. Nurse call not required (not patient care area).\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on E-002/E-201 and low voltage requirements. 2 access points shown on plan plus security/data outlets at workstations.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Coordinate with hospital IT department for standards. Access points shown on reflected ceiling plan at security and vestibule areas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"28-01\",\n      \"category\": \"Electronic Safety and Security\",\n      \"description\": \"Fire Alarm\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Fire alarm system modifications including: new smoke detectors for new room configuration; heat detectors at appropriate locations; manual pull stations; fire alarm horns/strobes; notification appliances; duct smoke detectors; monitor modules for sprinkler system; wiring and conduit; addressable devices; integration with existing hospital fire command center; ILSM coordination during installation. System must remain operational in occupied areas during construction.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on FA-101 fire alarm plan. Approximately 15-25 devices (smoke detectors, pull stations, horns/strobes).\", \n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Tie-in to existing hospital fire command center required. System must remain operational during construction per ILSM requirements. Coordinate with existing FA system architecture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item_code\": \"28-02\",\n      \"category\": \"Electronic Safety and Security\",\n      \"description\": \"Security Systems\",\n      \"unit\": \"LS\",\n      \"quantity\": 1,\n      \"scope_description\": \"Electronic security systems including: access control system (card readers, door position switches); intrusion detection; security cameras (360 cameras shown at entrance vestibule - 2 locations per E-101 and reflected ceiling plan); camera network video recorders; security control panels; security wiring and conduit; integration with 11-01 security equipment. Low voltage cabling for weapon detection system. Coordinate with MG Engineering design.\",\n      \"calculation_method\": \"Lump sum based on security requirements. 2-3 cameras visible on plans plus access control at security doors.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"notes\": \"Security design by MG Engineering D.P.C. Coordinate with hospital security department for integration with existing systems. Weapon detection system has dedicated low voltage cabling.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"takeoff_summary\": {\n    \"total_items\": 26,\n    \"high_confidence\": 6,\n    \"medium_confidence\": 17,\n    \"low_confidence\": 3,\n    \"key_assumptions\": [\n      \"No new toilet rooms in ambulance bay addition - scope is entrance/security area only\",\n      \"Existing panel CEHDP-A capacity must be verified for ACU-1 load (13kVA)\",\n      \"Ballistic panels and glazing per door schedule A-701\",\n      \"Light fixture quantities per Note 17 require Contractor verification\",\n      \"ACU-1 ductwork routing must coordinate with canopy structural steel\",\n      \"Fire alarm and sprinkler systems tie into existing hospital infrastructure\",\n      \"Multiple emergency power branches require ATS coordination\",\n      \"Asbestos abatement is prerequisite to all other demolition work\",\n      \"Weapon detection system at main entrance is specialized security equipment\",\n      \"No medical gas piping - this is not a patient treatment area\"\n    ],\n    \"critical_coordination_items\": [\n      \"MEP-01: ACU-1 ductwork vs structural steel canopy routing\",\n      \"MEP-03: Emergency power coordination with multiple transfer switches\", \n      \"MEP-04: Weapon detection system power and low voltage cabling paths\",\n      \"Sprinkler coverage coordination with ballistic glazing in vestibule\",\n      \"ICRA/ILSM requirements during all phases of construction\",\n      \"Fire alarm tie-in to existing hospital fire command center\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063279056}}
