{"type":"message","id":"dffcb0c7","parentId":"cfb3ba17","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:44.279Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BHKXfXruKj5pgYu9uiLS7S","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"project\": \"HHC Bellevue Hospital - Ambulance Drop Off Renovation\",\n  \"extraction_note\": \"Ambulance bay areas - not traditional room numbering\",\n  \"areas\": [\n    {\n      \"area_id\": \"AMB-01\",\n      \"area_name\": \"Ambulance Court\",\n      \"description\": \"Ambulance drop-off and pickup area\",\n      \"sheet\": \"A-101\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"area_id\": \"AMB-02\",\n      \"area_name\": \"Security Entrance Vestibule\",\n      \"description\": \"Weapon detection and security screening\",\n      \"sheet\": \"A-101\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"area_id\": \"AMB-03\",\n      \"area_name\": \"Decontamination Area\",\n      \"description\": \"Patient decontamination facilities\",\n      \"sheet\": \"A-101\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"area_id\": \"AMB-04\",\n      \"area_name\": \"Cart Wash Alcove\",\n      \"description\": \"Equipment cart washing station\",\n      \"sheet\": \"A-102\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"area_id\": \"AMB-05\",\n      \"area_name\": \"NYPD Security Pickup\",\n      \"description\": \"Police transfer area\",\n      \"sheet\": \"A-102\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"area_id\": \"AMB-06\",\n      \"area_name\": \"Canopy Structure\",\n      \"description\": \"Ambulance canopy and supporting structure\",\n      \"sheet\": \"S-101\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"room_data_pending\": \"True - Detailed room schedule extraction needed from A-701, A-801\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063284277}}
{"type":"message","id":"0c53d030","parentId":"dffcb0c7","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:14:54.597Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me look at a few more critical drawings for quantities I still need to verify - specifically the structural framing plan, foundation plan, and the plumbing roof plan for roof drains."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AxB6UpZhSJkGh3mzqMnhZR","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_086.png","prompt":"This is S-101 Canopy Framing Plan for Bellevue Hospital. Extract ALL structural steel members with sizes (W shapes, HSS, channels), their lengths, grid dimensions, and overall canopy dimensions. Count all columns/posts. List every beam and its size."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01EUftnG9pPtuBhLfsS36Sub","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_066.png","prompt":"This is P-102 Plumbing Roof Plan. Count ALL roof drains and overflow drains shown. Note their sizes and locations. I need an exact count of roof drains for the bid."}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01AzTWrHCSz1TgMophc4AoKR","name":"image","arguments":{"image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_079.png","prompt":"This is FO-101 Foundation Plan. Extract ALL foundation elements: pile caps (count and sizes), grade beams, slab dimensions, and any area/dimension callouts. Count every pile cap and pile."}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":454,"cacheRead":77882,"cacheWrite":4563,"totalTokens":82900,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.01135,"cacheRead":0.038940999999999996,"cacheWrite":0.028518750000000002,"total":0.07881474999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770063284279}}
{"type":"message","id":"57408baa","parentId":"0c53d030","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:15:00.110Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01AxB6UpZhSJkGh3mzqMnhZR","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This image is **not** a structural canopy framing plan. It is a **Fire Sprinkler Hydraulics Calculation Program** output (Elite Software) for the \"H+H Bellevue ED Ambulance Bay Addition,\" showing pipe segment flow data, node pressures, and hydraulic calculations.\n\nThere are no structural steel members, W shapes, HSS, channels, columns, beams, or grid dimensions in this document."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_086.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063300105}}
{"type":"message","id":"20039563","parentId":"57408baa","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:15:10.482Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01EUftnG9pPtuBhLfsS36Sub","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This drawing is **P-100.00 - Underground Plumbing Plan**, not P-102 Plumbing Roof Plan. It shows underground/cellar-level plumbing with sanitary and storm piping connections.\n\nThere are **no roof drains or overflow drains** shown on this sheet. The storm note references connecting new storm pipe to the existing storm system, but the actual roof drain locations would be on a separate roof plan sheet (P-102).\n\nFrom the **Storm System Notes** visible on this drawing, key info for your bid:\n\n- **No drains on this project exceed a coverage of 10,000 square feet** (Note 8)\n- A **4\" relief/overflow drain** is required where the maximum water level could equal 8\" above the roof membrane (Note 2)\n- Drains must be minimum **3 ft from roof's edge**, max 50 ft travel distance, spacing not more than 250 ft (Note 5)\n- Controlled flow roof drain system per NYC Plumbing Code\n\nYou'll need the **P-102 Plumbing Roof Plan** sheet for the actual roof drain count and sizes."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_066.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063310476}}
{"type":"message","id":"2593aa3b","parentId":"20039563","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:15:18.244Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01AzTWrHCSz1TgMophc4AoKR","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is **not** a foundation plan. This is sheet **SP-401.00 – Sprinkler Details (Sheet 1 of 2)** for the H+H Bellevue ED Ambulance Bay Addition project.\n\nThe sheet contains sprinkler-related details only:\n\n1. Typical Concealed Pendent Sprinkler Type\n2. Typical Upright Sprinkler Type\n3. Typical Hanger Detail\n4. Pipe Sleeves Thru Wall\n5. Pipe Penetration in Fire-Rated GWB or Plaster Partition\n6. Sprinkler Head Location\n7. Installation Details of Sidewall Sprinkler Head\n\nThere are **no foundation elements** (pile caps, piles, grade beams, slabs, or foundation dimensions) on this sheet."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_079.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063318237}}
