{"type":"message","id":"4ba58c48","parentId":"22f50054","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:15:59.141Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_016mCuDeKKUeooXuT3GKRyTa","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Sheet Number: **FO-201**\n\n**Title:** TYPICAL FOUNDATION DETAILS\n\n**Project:** H+H Bellevue — ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n\n---\n\n**Important Note:** This is **not a structural steel drawing**. This sheet contains **concrete foundation and reinforcement details**, not structural steel framing. It shows:\n\n- Typical reinforcing at openings and misc details (Detail N)\n- Horizontal section showing wall reinforcement placement (Detail O)\n- Typical one-way slab detail (Detail P)\n- Typical slab penetration sleeve detail (Detail Q)\n- Typical concrete pad detail (Detail R)\n- Foundation/buttress cross-wall sections\n\n**There are no structural steel members, steel columns/posts, or canopy dimensions on this sheet.**\n\nThe canopy steel framing (columns, beams, sizes, lengths, overall canopy dimensions) would typically be found on sheets like **S-series** (structural steel plans/elevations/details), not on this foundation details sheet.\n\nTo get the information you're requesting, you would need sheets such as:\n- **Structural steel framing plan** (canopy layout, member sizes, bay dimensions)\n- **Steel elevations/sections** (column heights, beam spans)\n- **Steel details** (connections, member schedules)"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_116.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770063359135}}
