{"type":"message","id":"fa0a5d0d","parentId":"5f772aec","timestamp":"2026-02-02T20:21:53.417Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create the comprehensive takeoff report."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Jh6mX8Gd55m4bQ81PxgZfW","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/takeoff/TAKEOFF_REPORT.md","content":"# QUANTITY TAKEOFF REPORT\n## HHC Bellevue Hospital — ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n### Project #11202402 | 462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016\n\n**Prepared:** 2026-06-19  \n**Architect:** ARRAY Architects (Project No. 6629)  \n**Structural Engineer:** Yimaki A. Senik, P.E.  \n**MEP Engineer:** Diverse Engineering PLLC  \n**Security Consultant:** MG Engineering D.P.C.  \n**Environmental:** Environmental Planning Management  \n**Issue:** Issued Solution for Bid — 09/25/25  \n\n---\n\n## PROJECT OVERVIEW\n\nSingle-story ambulance bay addition at Bellevue Hospital Emergency Department. The project includes:\n- **5 new rooms** totaling ~592 SF of interior floor area\n- **New canopy structure** (~485 SF) over ambulance drop-off\n- **Ballistic-resistant security features** (Level 3 throughout)\n- **Active hospital environment** requiring ICRA/ILSM compliance\n\n### Room Summary\n\n| Room | Area (SF) | Ceiling Type | Ceiling Ht | Floor | Walls |\n|------|-----------|-------------|------------|-------|-------|\n| Cart Wash | 212 | C-2 Gypsum | 9'-0\" | PE-2 Stonclad-UR Pewter | SWC-1 Stonglaze (all walls) |\n| Security Station | 82 | C-1 ACT | 10'-0\" | PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 | PT/W-1 & PT/W-2 tile + P-1 paint |\n| NYPD Security Pickup | 50 | C-1 ACT | 10'-0\" | PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 | P-1 epoxy paint (all walls) |\n| Entrance Vestibule | 207 | C-2 Gypsum | 10'-0\" | PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 | P-1 epoxy paint |\n| Cart Alcove | 41 | C-1 ACT | 9'-6\" | PE-1 Stonres-RTZ-2 | PWP-1 (N/S) + P-1 (E/W) |\n| **TOTAL** | **592** | | | | |\n\n---\n\n## QUANTIFIED BID ITEMS (Non-LS)\n\n### Item 28 — Concrete Work (030050) — **592 SF**\n- **Source:** A-101, FO-101, FO-200, FO-300\n- **Scope:** 12\" slab-on-grade, #6@12\" OC double mat, 4,000 PSI concrete\n- **Breakdown:** Cart Wash 212 SF + Security 82 SF + NYPD 50 SF + Vestibule 207 SF + Cart Alcove 41 SF\n- **Also includes:** Pile caps (~12 CY), grade beams GB-1 (2.7 CY) & GB-2 (4.2 CY), DB-1 (0.7 CY)\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\n\n### Item 30 — Cast Underlayment (035416) — **592 SF**\n- **Source:** A-801\n- **Scope:** Self-leveling underlayment over SOG for poured epoxy flooring in all 5 rooms\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 31 — Unit Masonry (042000) — **85 LF**\n- **Source:** A-101, A-201, A-223, A-224\n- **Scope:** New brick veneer to match existing on new exterior walls\n- **Breakdown:** BES-05 brick on CFMF (~55 LF) + BES-10 brick on CMU (~30 LF)\n- **Wall face area:** ~485 SF at avg 5.7' exposed height\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 32 — Structural Steel Framing (051200) — **350 LF**\n- **Source:** S-101, S-200, S-201\n- **Scope:** Canopy framing: W8x10 beams, W6x12 secondary, HSS6x2, C6x13, L4x3.5 lintels\n- **Total weight:** ~8,750 lbs. T.O.S. at EL 27'-0\". A992/A572 Gr50.\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 36 — Sheathing (061600) — **485 SF**\n- **Source:** A-223, A-224, EN-300\n- **Scope:** 5/8\" DensGlass exterior sheathing at new exterior walls (BES-05, BES-08)\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 38 — Self-Adhering Sheet Waterproofing (071326) — **592 SF**\n- **Source:** A-223, FO-200\n- **Scope:** Underslab waterproofing membrane at SOG. Foundation wall WP (~285 SF) additional.\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 39 — Thermal Insulation (072100) — **1,170 SF**\n- **Source:** A-223, A-224, EN-001, EN-002\n- **Scope:** Walls: 2\" polyiso R-8.5 (485 SF) + 3.5\" batt R-13 (485 SF). Slab edge R-15 (195 SF). Additional at roof (~485 SF) counted under roofing.\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 40 — Air Barriers (072700) — **485 SF**\n- **Source:** A-223, A-224, EN-300\n- **Scope:** Air/water-resistive barrier on all new exterior walls over DensGlass sheathing\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 41 — Fluid-Applied Protected Membrane Roofing (075556) — **485 SF**\n- **Source:** A-303, A-501\n- **Scope:** PMMA liquid-applied roofing at canopy (~37' x 13'). R-33 polyiso (5.5\" min) + cover board + membrane. 1/4\"/ft slope to 4 roof drains.\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 46 — Hollow Metal Doors and Frames (081113) — **2 EA**\n- **Source:** A-701 Door Schedule\n- **Doors:**\n  - ED-1-01: Cart Wash, 5'-0\" x 7'-0\", single, HM/TF, HW set 1.0\n  - ED-1-09: Entrance Vestibule, 6'-0\" x 7'-0\", pair, HM/TF, no HW set listed\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\n\n### Item 47 — Access Doors and Panels (083100) — **6 EA** ⚠️\n- **Source:** A-501 keynotes C2, C3, C6\n- **Scope:** Metal and GWB access panels for MEP access above ceilings\n- **⚠️ WARNING:** Note 10 on A-501: \"Access panels are not quantified or indicated on the drawings.\" Contractor to verify in field. Estimated 6 EA.\n- **Confidence:** LOW\n\n### Item 48 — Aluminum-Framed Entrances and Storefronts (084113) — **3 EA**\n- **Source:** A-101, A-200, A-704\n- **Systems:**\n  1. Exterior ballistic storefront at main entry (with sliding doors ED-1-06 & ED-1-07)\n  2. Interior ballistic storefront at Security Station\n  3. NYPD Security Pickup storefront\n- **All:** Thermally broken, ballistic Level 3. BOD: US Bullet Proofing USAW400\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 49 — Glazing (088000) — **375 SF**\n- **Source:** A-701, A-200, A-704\n- **Breakdown:** ED-1-02 (27), ED-1-03 (23), ED-1-04 (23), ED-1-06 sliding (115), ED-1-07 sliding (115), ED-1-08 (27), sidelites/transoms (~45) = 375 SF\n- **All ballistic Level 3**\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 50 — Security Glazing (088853) — **110 SF** ⚠️\n- **Source:** A-101, A-400, A-704\n- **Scope:** Additional security glazing at storefront sidelites, transaction windows, fixed panels beyond door glazing\n- **⚠️ VERIFY** with MG Engineering security consultant\n- **Confidence:** LOW\n\n### Item 52 — Gypsum Board Assemblies (092116) — **2,850 SF**\n- **Source:** A-101, A-701, A-801\n- **Breakdown:** Walls (both sides): 1,453 SF net x 2 = 2,258 SF + C-2 GWB ceilings (Cart Wash 212 + Vestibule 207 = ~592 SF) = ~2,850 SF\n- **Material:** 5/8\" Type X GWB per partition types\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 53 — Tiling (093000) — **145 SF**\n- **Source:** A-801, A-400\n- **Scope:** 2CM porcelain tile walls at Security Station only:\n  - PT/W-1: Silestone Cala Blue, north wall (~65 SF)\n  - PT/W-2: Dekton Kreta, south wall (~80 SF)\n- **Full height to 10' ceiling. Metal trim MT-1 at corners.**\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 55 — Special Wall Surfacing (097700) — **531 SF**\n- **Source:** A-801\n- **Scope:** SWC-1 Stonhard Stonglaze VSR Ash Grey on all 4 walls of Cart Wash\n- **Calculation:** ~59 LF perimeter x 9' height = 531 SF gross (less 35 SF door = ~496 SF net)\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 56 — Painting and Coating (099000) — **2,100 SF**\n- **Source:** A-801\n- **Breakdown:**\n  - P-1 walls: Security (175) + NYPD (230) + Vestibule (420) + Cart Alcove (182) = 1,007 SF\n  - P-2/P-3 ceilings: Cart Wash P-3 (212) + Vestibule P-2 (207) = 419 SF\n  - Misc/touch-up: ~674 SF\n- **Paint:** P-1 Benjamin Moore Epoxy Mountain Peak White 2148-70\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 57 — Wall and Door Protection (102600) — **104 SF**\n- **Source:** A-801\n- **Scope:** PWP-1 INPRO Palladium White Sand, 60\" high, N and S walls of Cart Alcove (~63 SF) + door protection (~41 SF)\n- **Includes:** Corner guard CG-1\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\n\n### Item 58 — Ballistics Resistant Panels (102641) — **250 SF** ⚠️\n- **Source:** A-701, A-400, A-704\n- **Scope:** 7/16\" fiberglass ballistic panels at partition types 7D/7E, floor to 4\" above ceiling\n- **Calculation:** ~25 LF x 10' height = 250 SF\n- **⚠️ VERIFY** exact wall lengths on A-101\n- **Confidence:** LOW\n\n### Item 59 — Fire Protection Specialties (104400) — **4 EA (bid as SF)** ⚠️\n- **Source:** A-101\n- **Scope:** 4 fire extinguisher cabinets per code travel distance requirements\n- **⚠️ NOTE:** Bid sheet unit is SF but this is likely EA. If SF, ~8 SF (2 SF face area each). Clarify with Owner.\n- **Confidence:** LOW\n\n### Item 60 — Removable Flood Barriers (107119.16) — **1 EA**\n- **Source:** A-101, G-004\n- **Scope:** 2' high deployable flood barrier system, Flood Risk America (Flood Defense Group) EZ Flood Panels or equal\n- **Location:** Ambulance bay entrance, project in flood zone per G-004\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\n\n### Item 61 — Countertops (123600) — **18 SF** ⚠️\n- **Source:** A-702, A-400\n- **Scope:** Solid surface countertop at Security Station transaction counter\n- **Calculation:** ~12 LF x 1.5' deep = 18 SF. Includes support brackets.\n- **⚠️ VERIFY** exact dimensions from A-702 details\n- **Confidence:** LOW\n\n### Item 62 — Bicycle Racks (129313) — **1 EA**\n- **Source:** A-101, A-201\n- **Scope:** Tubular ground-mounted bicycle rack per spec 129313, exterior near ambulance bay entrance\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\n\n### Item 84 — Roof Drains (221426) — **4 EA**\n- **Source:** P-102, A-501, A-303\n- **Scope:** 4 EA roof drains (4\" diameter) each paired with overflow drain (4\" diameter) = 4 RD + 4 OD\n- **Note:** Existing drain(s) reinstalled per A-501 keynote A0. Controlled flow per NYC Plumbing Code.\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\n\n---\n\n## LUMP SUM ITEMS — SCOPE NOTES\n\n### Division 01 — General Requirements (Items 3-25)\nStandard general conditions for NYC H+H hospital project. Key considerations:\n- **ICRA Class III/IV** infection control during construction\n- **ILSM** - maintain fire/life safety during construction\n- Hospital occupied throughout - noise/vibration restrictions\n- NYC DOB permits, FDNY coordination\n- Hazmat abatement prerequisite\n\n### Item 26 — Selective Demolition\nDemo of existing ambulance drop-off area (~3,200 SF): existing walls, ceilings, floors, doors, MEP. Weathering steel panels carefully removed for Owner reuse. Active hospital - full ICRA barriers.\n\n### Item 27 — Asbestos Removal\nComplete ACM abatement per environmental survey. NYC DEP compliance. Must be completed BEFORE any construction demolition.\n\n### Item 29 — Post Installed Anchors\nConnections to existing building at expansion joint and structural tie-in locations.\n\n### Items 33-34 — Cold Formed Metal Framing & Metal Fabrication\nCFMF: All interior partitions (3-5/8\" and 6\" studs at 16\" OC) and exterior backup walls. GWB ceiling framing.\nMetal Fab: Shelf angles (~145 LF), lintels (6 EA), HSS posts for storefront (4 EA), bollards (6 EA), canopy fascia/soffit (~78 LF), gutters (~42 LF).\n\n### Items 35, 37 — Rough Carpentry & Architectural Woodwork\nRough: ~200 BF FR-treated blocking for storefront, equipment, casework.\nWoodwork: Security desk with phenolic panels, ~28 LF total casework.\n\n### Items 42-45 — Roof Specialties, Fire Protection, Firestopping, Sealants\nRoof: Fascia/coping (~78 LF), gutters (~42 LF), roof edge flashing, expansion joints.\nFire: SFRM on ~8,750 lbs structural steel.\nFirestopping: ~30-50 penetrations through rated assemblies.\nSealants: ~485 LF total (storefront, doors, joints).\n\n### Item 51 — Flooring Preparation\nSubstrate prep for poured epoxy in all 5 rooms (592 SF). Grinding, patching, moisture testing, primer.\n\n### Item 54 — Acoustical Ceiling\nArmstrong 3214 Optima Health 24\"x24\", Prelude 15/16\" grid: Security (82 SF), NYPD (50 SF), Cart Alcove (41 SF) = **173 SF**. Correctional-grade secure type required.\n\n### Items 63-71 — Sprinkler\nWet/dry pipe modifications for ~3,200 SF + canopy. ~30-50 heads. Tie-in to existing hospital system. NFPA 13 compliance. Hydraulic calcs provided (pages 81-97).\n\n### Items 72-83 — Plumbing\nDomestic CW/HW, sanitary, storm drainage. No new fixtures (no toilet rooms). Cart Wash floor drains and hose bibbs. Underground per P-100.\n\n### Items 85-107 — Mechanical\nPrimary: ACU-1 (13 kVA, 3-phase, roof-mounted). Air curtains at entrance. Unit heaters. ~1,500-2,500 SF ductwork. DDC controls with BAS integration. ⚠️ ACU-1 routing must coordinate with canopy structural steel.\n\n### Items 108-128 — Electrical\nConnection to existing CEHDP-A (480/277V, 2000A bus). New panels: LP-1, CDP-1/2/A, CDPE-1, FA-5-A/B. ~70-75 light fixtures (all LED). ~30-40 hospital-grade receptacles. Weapon detection dedicated circuits. Emergency power (Life Safety + Critical + Equipment branches).\n\n### Item 129 — Fire Alarm\n~15-25 devices. Tie-in to existing fire command center. ILSM during installation. Addressable system.\n\n### Items 130-132 — Other\nCatch-all: signage (illuminated EMERGENCY), security cameras/equipment, weapon detection system, backboard storage, decontamination equipment support.\n\n---\n\n## FLAGS & RISKS\n\n### ⚠️ HIGH PRIORITY\n1. **Access Panels (Item 47):** \"Not quantified or indicated on the drawings\" per Note 10. Contractor must coordinate with MEP and verify in field. Budget for 6-10 EA minimum.\n2. **Security Glazing (Item 50):** Exact SF unclear — verify with MG Engineering security consultant.\n3. **Ballistic Panels (Item 58):** Exact wall lengths for partition types 7D/7E need field verification.\n4. **Fire Protection Specialties (Item 59):** Unit mismatch — bid sheet says SF but items are EA. Clarify with Owner.\n5. **ACU-1 Routing (MEP-01):** Ductwork must clear structural canopy steel — potential conflict.\n6. **Emergency Power (MEP-03):** Multiple ATS coordination required for Life Safety/Critical/Equipment branches.\n\n### ⚠️ MEDIUM PRIORITY\n7. **Countertops (Item 61):** Limited dimensional data from A-702. Verify with shop drawings.\n8. **Masonry (Item 31):** Match existing brick — requires mockup/sample approval.\n9. **Flood Zone:** Project in flood zone per G-004. Verify if additional floodproofing beyond Item 60 barrier is required.\n10. **Asbestos (Item 27):** Exact ACM quantities require field survey verification.\n11. **Missing Door ED-1-05:** Not in schedule — verify intentional skip or omission.\n12. **Light Fixtures:** Note 17 states \"quantities to be confirmed by Contractor before pricing.\"\n\n### ℹ️ INFORMATION\n13. **Sheet Index Mapping:** Pages 77-134 are primarily sprinkler hydraulic calcs and structural/foundation/civil drawings. Sheet index JSON mapping is unreliable for these pages.\n14. **Unknown Pages (98-134):** Many classified as \"Unknown\" — majority are sprinkler hydraulic calculation reports.\n\n---\n\n## DATA SOURCES\n\n| Source | Sheet | Page | Content Used For |\n|--------|-------|------|-----------------|\n| A-101 | Construction Plan | 009 | Room layout, dimensions, doors, partitions |\n| A-200 | BES Schedule | 011 | Exterior wall/door assemblies |\n| A-201 | Elevations | 012 | Building heights, exterior materials |\n| A-221 | Building Section | 013 | Heights, wall assemblies |\n| A-223/224 | Wall Sections | 014-015 | Wall buildup, insulation, sheathing |\n| A-303 | Roof Details | 018 | Roof assembly, drain details |\n| A-400 | Interior Elevations | 020 | Security desk, wall finishes |\n| A-501 | RCP/Roof Plan | 021 | Ceiling types, roof drains, access panels |\n| A-701 | Door Schedule | 022 | 9 doors, partition types |\n| A-702 | Casework Details | 023 | Countertops, casework |\n| A-801 | Finish Schedule | 025 | All room finishes, materials |\n| AD-101 | Demo Plan | 008 | Demolition scope |\n| P-102 | Plumbing Roof | 068 | 4 roof drains + 4 overflow drains |\n| S-101 | Canopy Framing | 121 | Steel members, canopy dimensions |\n| FO-101 | Foundation Plan | (synth) | Pile caps, grade beams |\n| Specs | Full Text | — | Material specs, all CSI divisions |\n\n---\n\n## CONFIDENCE SUMMARY\n\n| Confidence | Count | Items |\n|-----------|-------|-------|\n| HIGH | 8 | #28, #46, #54, #60, #62, #84, #26, #51 |\n| MEDIUM | 15 | #30, #31, #32, #36, #38, #39, #40, #41, #48, #49, #52, #53, #55, #56, #57 |\n| LOW | 5 | #47, #50, #58, #59, #61 |\n| N/A (LS) | 104 | All lump sum items |\n\n**Overall takeoff confidence: MEDIUM** — 5 rooms in a relatively small addition with good drawing coverage. Low-confidence items are primarily specialties where drawings note \"Contractor to verify.\"\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":5718,"cacheRead":92385,"cacheWrite":11170,"totalTokens":109274,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.14295,"cacheRead":0.0461925,"cacheWrite":0.0698125,"total":0.25895999999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770063587829}}
